# Agente IA → living documentation

Whenever you add or change an **Agente IA / Asistente** feature in the same task, update [`docs/asistente-ia.md`](docs/asistente-ia.md) in the **same change**. Do not leave doc updates for “later”.

## Must update when touching

- New/changed tools → catalogue + **permiso** + **requiereConfirmacion**
- Permission, scope, or confirmation behaviour
- Hard restrictions / non-capabilities (SQL, web, admin, secrets, Calendar limits, etc.)
- Model, secrets, env, deploy scripts for the agent
- Schema / migrations (`ia_*`, `ultimo_acceso_en`, …)
- Admin panel (`/admin/agente-ia`) or user gastos UI
- Cost tracking / limits
- Known risks or gaps introduced by the change
- `resumen_periodo` shape: keep **nested** `personal` / `proyectos` / `comunicaciones` (+ `atribucion.reglas`). Do **not** reintroduce flat root aliases that mix “session user did X” with project-scope activity (`creadasEnPeriodo`, etc.). Update docs §6 Attribution scopes in the same change.

## Doc style

- Prefer English (matches current doc); keep tool/permission names exact as in code
- Prefer editing existing sections over appending vague notes
- If code and doc disagree, **fix the doc to match code**
- Mention branch/deploy caveats only if they still apply (`agenteia` / `dev-mst`, etc.)

## Do not

- Skip the doc for “small” tool tweaks
- Document unrelated portal features in this file
